# Copy to user-password.py, fill in, then: chmod 600 user-password.py
#
# This is a BOT PASSWORD, which is not a bot account. It is a second,
# scoped password on your own account, created at Special:BotPasswords.
# Edits still appear in page history as you; there is no separate account
# and no bot flag.
#
# Two reasons to use one rather than your account password:
#
#   1. MediaWiki deprecated main-account login via action=login. Pywikibot
#      picks the login method by looking for "@" in the username or the
#      password, so an account password that happens to contain an "@"
#      silently lands you on the deprecated path. A bot password is the
#      supported way to use action=login, and takes the guesswork out.
#   2. It is scoped to the grants you tick and revocable on its own, so
#      this file never holds the password to the account itself. Three
#      grants are enough: Basic rights, Edit existing pages, and Edit your
#      watchlist. See README.md.
#
# The suffix below is the name you gave the bot password, not the whole
# login name - Pywikibot joins them into "SpeakNigeria@yorubadict".

('SpeakNigeria', BotPassword('YorubaDict', 'the-32-character-string-shown-once'))
